{"key":"fe60aa5acb0c0960","source_file":"Potts Re.json","source_id":51399,"source_url":"concordance-retorsion-ppl-retorsio","term":"Retorsion","headwords":["Retorsion","Retort, To"],"latin":["Retorsio","Retorquere"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Retorsion"],"latin":["Retorsio"]},{"english":["Retort, To"],"latin":["Retorquere"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","DLW","DP","SE"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"829","subsection":"2"},"text":"(The penalty of) contorsions and retorsions...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DLW","section":"254","subsection":"2"},"text":"Like the retorsion of a spiral. DLW 263:2. CL 203.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DLW","section":"268","subsection":"2"},"text":"Cannot by any inversion or retorsion be reduced into a state opposite...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DP","section":"319","subsection":"4"},"text":"As the turning cannot be twisted back... he so remains to eternity. DP 338:7.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"2889","subsection":null},"text":"Retorting the evil upon them...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"2913","subsection":null},"text":"Evil is retorted upon (the evildoer)... for such as is the evil... such is the evil retorted upon him... They were the cause of this evil, and it was retorted upon them. SE 3037.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"3918","subsection":null},"text":"(A representation) of falsity by a retorsion of the forms.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"4097","subsection":null},"text":"As soon as they acted [upon her], she retorted herself...","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"retorsion","url":"/meta/potts/retorsion/"}